1
00:00:01,470 --> 00:00:08,870
Chapter 19 The library looked tranquil enough as I entered it, and the sibil,

2
00:00:09,599 --> 00:00:15,311
if sibil she were, was seated snugly enough in an easy chair at the chimney corner.

3
00:00:15,839 --> 00:00:22,150
She had on a red cloak and a black bonnet, or rather a broad-brimmed gypsy hat tied

4
00:00:22,150 --> 00:00:25,230
down with a striped hankerchief under her chin.

5
00:00:26,500 --> 00:00:28,910
An extinguished candle stood on the table.

6
00:00:30,059 --> 00:00:31,550
She was bending over the fire.

7
00:00:32,349 --> 00:00:35,103
And seemed reading in a little black book,

8
00:00:35,103 --> 00:00:39,031
like a prayer book by the light of the blaze.

9
00:00:39,279 --> 00:00:44,250
She muttered the words to herself, as most old women do while she read.

10
00:00:45,589 --> 00:00:48,169
She did not desist immediately on my entrance.

11
00:00:49,050 --> 00:00:51,389
It appeared she wished to finish a paragraph.

12
00:00:53,250 --> 00:00:57,447
I stood on the rug and warmed my hands, which were rather

13
00:00:57,447 --> 00:01:00,550
cold with sitting at a distance from the drawing room fire.

14
00:01:01,900 --> 00:01:05,389
I felt now as composed as ever I did in my life.

15
00:01:06,180 --> 00:01:11,330
There was nothing indeed in the gypsy's appearance to trouble one s calm.

16
00:01:12,900 --> 00:01:15,309
She shut her book and slowly looked up.

17
00:01:16,339 --> 00:01:20,216
Her hat brim partially shaded her face, yet I could

18
00:01:20,218 --> 00:01:23,349
see as she raised it that it was a strange one.

19
00:01:24,269 --> 00:01:25,970
It looked all brown and black.

20
00:01:26,989 --> 00:01:31,569
Elf locks bristled out from beneath a white band, which passed under her chin

21
00:01:32,120 --> 00:01:34,989
and came half over her cheeks, or rather jaws.

22
00:01:35,949 --> 00:01:39,949
Her eye confronted me at once, with a bold and direct gaze.

23
00:01:41,319 --> 00:01:45,552
Well, and you want your fortune told, she said, in a

24
00:01:45,552 --> 00:01:49,449
voice as decided as her glance, as harsh as her features.

25
00:01:50,500 --> 00:01:51,769
I don't care about it, mother.

26
00:01:52,470 --> 00:01:56,629
You may please yourself, but I ought to warn you I have no faith.

27
00:01:57,980 --> 00:01:59,750
It's like your impudence to say so.

28
00:02:00,529 --> 00:02:01,750
I expected it of you.

29
00:02:02,489 --> 00:02:04,870
I heard it in your step as you crossed the threshold.

30
00:02:05,830 --> 00:02:06,830
Did you?

31
00:02:07,169 --> 00:02:08,169
You've a quick ear.

32
00:02:09,010 --> 00:02:10,010
I have.

33
00:02:10,319 --> 00:02:12,230
And a quick eye and a quick brain.

34
00:02:13,220 --> 00:02:14,500
You need them all in your trade.

35
00:02:15,339 --> 00:02:18,849
I do, especially when I have customers like you to deal with.

36
00:02:19,529 --> 00:02:20,529
Why don't you tremble?

37
00:02:21,089 --> 00:02:22,089
I'm not cold.

38
00:02:22,800 --> 00:02:23,989
Why don't you turn pale?

39
00:02:24,949 --> 00:02:25,949
I am not sick.

40
00:02:26,589 --> 00:02:27,910
Why don't you consult my heart?

41
00:02:28,870 --> 00:02:29,930
I'm not silly.

42
00:02:30,709 --> 00:02:34,809
The old crone nishered a laugh under her bonnet and bandage.

43
00:02:35,750 --> 00:02:41,169
She then drew out a short black pipe, and lighting it began to smoke.

44
00:02:42,480 --> 00:02:47,389
Having indulged a while in this sedative, she raised her bent body, took the pipe

45
00:02:47,391 --> 00:02:51,510
from her lips, and while gazing steadily at the fire, said very deliberately.

46
00:02:52,949 --> 00:02:53,949
You are cold.

47
00:02:54,349 --> 00:02:55,349
You are sick.

48
00:02:55,650 --> 00:02:56,930
And you are silly.

49
00:02:58,160 --> 00:02:59,650
Prove it, I rejoined.

50
00:03:00,169 --> 00:03:01,529
I will, in few words.

51
00:03:02,349 --> 00:03:03,349
You are cold.

52
00:03:03,629 --> 00:03:04,629
Because you are alone.

53
00:03:05,349 --> 00:03:08,029
No contact strikes the fire from you that is in you.

54
00:03:08,750 --> 00:03:09,750
You are sick.

55
00:03:10,349 --> 00:03:13,491
Because the best of feelings, the highest and the

56
00:03:13,491 --> 00:03:16,531
sweetest given to man keeps far away from you.

57
00:03:16,730 --> 00:03:17,730
You are silly.

58
00:03:17,779 --> 00:03:21,989
Because, suffer as you may, you will not beckon it to approach.

59
00:03:22,989 --> 00:03:26,449
Nor will you stir one step to meet it where it waits you.

60
00:03:27,860 --> 00:03:33,629
She again put her short black pipe to her lips and renewed her smoking with vigor.

61
00:03:35,470 --> 00:03:37,957
You might say all that to almost anyone who you

62
00:03:37,957 --> 00:03:40,989
knew lived as a solitary dependent in a great house.

63
00:03:42,364 --> 00:03:47,349
I might say it to almost anyone, but would it be true of almost anyone?

64
00:03:48,709 --> 00:03:56,709
In my circumstances, yes, just so in your circumstances, but find me another

65
00:03:56,959 --> 00:03:58,470
precisely placed as you are.

66
00:03:59,639 --> 00:04:01,449
It would be easy to find you thousands.

67
00:04:02,680 --> 00:04:04,269
You could scarcely find me one.

68
00:04:05,559 --> 00:04:08,510
If you knew it, you are peculiarly situated.

69
00:04:09,110 --> 00:04:10,209
Very near happiness.

70
00:04:10,790 --> 00:04:13,029
Yes, within reach of it.

71
00:04:14,190 --> 00:04:15,730
The materials are all prepared.

72
00:04:16,669 --> 00:04:19,029
There only wants a movement to combine them.

73
00:04:20,129 --> 00:04:21,949
Chance laid them somewhat apart.

74
00:04:22,989 --> 00:04:26,129
Let them be once approached and bliss results.

75
00:04:27,690 --> 00:04:29,330
I don't understand enigmas.

76
00:04:30,169 --> 00:04:32,410
I never could guess a riddle in my life.

77
00:04:33,769 --> 00:04:36,769
If you wish me to speak more plainly, show me your palm.

78
00:04:37,980 --> 00:04:40,230
And I must cross it with silver, I suppose?

79
00:04:41,440 --> 00:04:44,209
To be sure, I gave her a shilling.

80
00:04:45,319 --> 00:04:48,875
She put it into an old stocking foot which she took out

81
00:04:48,875 --> 00:04:52,169
of her pocket and having tied it round and returned it.

82
00:04:52,629 --> 00:04:54,730
She told me to hold out my hand.

83
00:04:55,430 --> 00:04:56,430
I did.

84
00:04:56,919 --> 00:05:00,790
She approached her face to the palm and poured over it without touching it.

85
00:05:02,089 --> 00:05:04,169
It is too fine, said she.

86
00:05:05,190 --> 00:05:08,569
I can make nothing of such a hand as that, almost without lines.

87
00:05:09,449 --> 00:05:11,110
Besides, what is in a palm?

88
00:05:11,970 --> 00:05:13,250
Destiny is not written there.

89
00:05:14,139 --> 00:05:15,849
I believe you, said I.

90
00:05:16,550 --> 00:05:17,690
No, she continued.

91
00:05:18,639 --> 00:05:23,629
It is in the face, on the forehead, about the eyes, in the lines of the mouth,

92
00:05:24,589 --> 00:05:26,529
kneel and lift up your head.

93
00:05:27,809 --> 00:05:31,849
Ah, now you are coming to reality, I said, as I obeyed her.

94
00:05:32,690 --> 00:05:35,489
I shall begin to put some faith in you presently.

95
00:05:36,970 --> 00:05:39,029
I knelt within half a yard of her.

96
00:05:39,790 --> 00:05:43,910
She stirred the fire so that a ripple of light broke from the disturbed coal.

97
00:05:44,690 --> 00:05:48,870
The glare, however, as she sat, only through her face into deeper shadow,

98
00:05:49,489 --> 00:05:51,230
mine it illumined.

99
00:05:53,555 --> 00:05:56,949
I wonder with what feelings you came to me tonight.

100
00:05:58,150 --> 00:06:03,269
She said, when she had examined me a while, I wonder what thoughts are busy in

101
00:06:03,271 --> 00:06:06,870
your heart during all the hours you sit in your under room with the fine people

102
00:06:06,870 --> 00:06:09,629
flitting before you like shapes in a magic lantern.

103
00:06:10,815 --> 00:06:15,309
Just as little sympathetic communion passing between you and them as if they

104
00:06:15,311 --> 00:06:20,529
were really mere shadows of human forms and not the actual substance.

105
00:06:22,949 --> 00:06:28,169
I feel tired often, sleepy sometimes, but seldom sad.

106
00:06:30,160 --> 00:06:33,605
Then you have some secret hope to bore you up

107
00:06:33,607 --> 00:06:37,571
and please you with whispers of the future.

108
00:06:38,459 --> 00:06:39,459
Not I.

109
00:06:40,309 --> 00:06:45,790
The utmost I hope is to save money enough out of my earnings, to set up a school

110
00:06:45,790 --> 00:06:48,910
someday in a little house rented by myself.

111
00:06:50,459 --> 00:06:53,786
A mean nutriment for the spirit to exist on, and

112
00:06:53,786 --> 00:06:56,709
sitting in that window seat you see I know your habits.

113
00:06:57,779 --> 00:06:59,381
You have learned them from the servants.

114
00:07:00,489 --> 00:07:02,370
Ah, you think yourself sharp?

115
00:07:03,050 --> 00:07:04,389
Well, perhaps I have.

116
00:07:05,069 --> 00:07:08,910
To speak truth, I have an acquaintance with one of them, Mrs. Pool.

117
00:07:10,455 --> 00:07:12,569
I started to my feet when I heard the name.

118
00:07:13,750 --> 00:07:14,209
You have?

119
00:07:14,589 --> 00:07:15,589
Have you?

120
00:07:16,010 --> 00:07:17,010
Thought I.

121
00:07:17,669 --> 00:07:20,650
There is deablery in the business after all then.

122
00:07:22,349 --> 00:07:25,230
Don't be alarmed, continued the strange being.

123
00:07:26,180 --> 00:07:29,029
She is a safe hand, Mrs. Pool, close and quiet.

124
00:07:29,730 --> 00:07:31,569
Anyone may oppose confidence in her.

125
00:07:32,489 --> 00:07:36,404
But, as I was saying, sitting in that window seat,

126
00:07:36,404 --> 00:07:39,370
do you think of nothing but your future school?

127
00:07:40,360 --> 00:07:42,815
Have you no present interest in any of the company

128
00:07:42,815 --> 00:07:45,571
who occupy the sofas and chairs before you?

129
00:07:46,269 --> 00:07:48,110
Is there not one face you study?

130
00:07:48,940 --> 00:07:52,949
One figure whose movements you follow with at least curiosity.

131
00:07:54,150 --> 00:07:56,529
I like to observe all the faces and all the figures.

132
00:07:58,000 --> 00:08:01,750
But do you never single one from the rest, or it may be two?

133
00:08:02,989 --> 00:08:03,989
I do frequently.

134
00:08:04,750 --> 00:08:11,150
When the gestures or looks of a pair seem telling a tale, it amuses me to watch them.

135
00:08:11,750 --> 00:08:13,769
What tale do you like best to hear?

136
00:08:15,720 --> 00:08:17,529
Oh, I have not much choice.

137
00:08:18,489 --> 00:08:21,889
They generally run on the same theme, courtship, and

138
00:08:21,889 --> 00:08:25,589
promise to end in the same catastrophe, marriage.

139
00:08:27,235 --> 00:08:29,089
And do you like that monotonous theme?

140
00:08:30,550 --> 00:08:33,730
Positively, I don't care about it, it is nothing to me.

141
00:08:34,970 --> 00:08:36,069
Nothing to you.

142
00:08:36,970 --> 00:08:42,550
When a lady, young and full of life and health, charming with beauty and endowed

143
00:08:42,550 --> 00:08:48,470
with the gifts of rank and fortune, sits and smiles in the eyes of a gentleman you.

144
00:08:48,709 --> 00:08:49,709
I what?

145
00:08:50,690 --> 00:08:51,690
You know.

146
00:08:52,309 --> 00:08:53,790
And perhaps think well of.

147
00:08:55,620 --> 00:08:57,209
I don't know the gentleman here.

148
00:08:57,790 --> 00:09:00,389
I have scarcely interchanged a syllable with one of them.

149
00:09:01,199 --> 00:09:05,709
And as to thinking well of them, I consider some respectable and stately

150
00:09:05,711 --> 00:09:10,730
and middle-aged, and others young, dashing, handsome and lively.

151
00:09:11,910 --> 00:09:17,050
But certainly, they are all at liberty, to be the recipients of whose smiles they

152
00:09:17,050 --> 00:09:23,411
please, without my feeling disposed to consider the transaction of any moment to me.

153
00:09:24,069 --> 00:09:25,669
You don't know the gentleman here.

154
00:09:26,410 --> 00:09:28,930
You have not exchanged a syllable with one of them.

155
00:09:29,930 --> 00:09:32,029
Will you say that of the master of the house?

156
00:09:33,500 --> 00:09:34,650
He is not at home.

157
00:09:36,150 --> 00:09:39,910
A profound remark, a most ingenious quibble.

158
00:09:40,730 --> 00:09:44,910
He went to milk-coat this morning, and will be back here tonight or tomorrow.

159
00:09:45,864 --> 00:09:49,949
Does that circumstance exclude him from the list of your acquaintance?

160
00:09:50,690 --> 00:09:53,650
Blot him, as it were, out of existence.

161
00:09:55,809 --> 00:09:58,813
No, but I can scarcely see what Mr. Rochester

162
00:09:58,813 --> 00:10:02,091
has to do with the theme you had introduced.

163
00:10:03,720 --> 00:10:09,510
I was talking of ladies smiling in the eyes of gentleman, and of late so many

164
00:10:09,510 --> 00:10:13,610
smiles have been shared into Mr. Rochester's eyes that they overflow,

165
00:10:14,370 --> 00:10:16,470
like two cups filled above the brim.

166
00:10:17,309 --> 00:10:18,790
Have you never remarked that?

167
00:10:20,480 --> 00:10:24,889
Mr. Rochester has a right to enjoy the society of his guests.

168
00:10:26,089 --> 00:10:30,105
No question about his right, but have you never observed

169
00:10:30,105 --> 00:10:33,569
that of all the tales told here about matrimony?

170
00:10:34,559 --> 00:10:39,690
Mr. Rochester has been favored with the most lively and the most continuous.

171
00:10:41,385 --> 00:10:45,069
The eagerness of a listener quickens the tongue of a narrator.

172
00:10:46,360 --> 00:10:52,069
I said this rather to myself than to the gypsy, whose strange talk, voice manner,

173
00:10:52,790 --> 00:10:55,349
had by this time wrapped me in a kind of dream.

174
00:10:56,370 --> 00:10:59,836
One unexpected sentence came from her lips after

175
00:10:59,836 --> 00:11:03,949
another, till I got involved in a web of mystification.

176
00:11:04,949 --> 00:11:09,277
And wondered what unseen spirit had been sitting for weeks by

177
00:11:09,277 --> 00:11:14,029
my heart watching its workings and taking record of every pulse.

178
00:11:15,519 --> 00:11:22,190
Eagerness of a listener repeated she, yes, Mr. Rochester has sat by the hour,

179
00:11:22,750 --> 00:11:25,841
his ear inclined to the fascinating lips that

180
00:11:25,843 --> 00:11:29,190
took such delight in their task of communicating.

181
00:11:29,809 --> 00:11:32,821
And Mr. Rochester was so willing to receive and

182
00:11:32,822 --> 00:11:35,391
looked so grateful for the past time given him.

183
00:11:36,050 --> 00:11:37,050
You have noticed this?

184
00:11:38,010 --> 00:11:39,010
Grateful.

185
00:11:39,730 --> 00:11:42,669
I cannot remember detecting gratitude in his face.

186
00:11:44,190 --> 00:11:45,190
Detecting.

187
00:11:45,419 --> 00:11:46,629
You have analyzed then.

188
00:11:47,370 --> 00:11:49,510
And what did you detect if not gratitude?

189
00:11:50,449 --> 00:11:51,449
I said nothing.

190
00:11:52,309 --> 00:11:54,069
You have seen love, have you not?

191
00:11:54,809 --> 00:11:59,449
And looking forward, you have seen him married, and beheld his bride happy?

192
00:12:00,510 --> 00:12:02,330
Huff, not exactly.

193
00:12:03,190 --> 00:12:05,949
Your witch's skill is rather at fault sometimes.

194
00:12:07,589 --> 00:12:09,010
What the devil have you seen then?

195
00:12:10,349 --> 00:12:11,349
Never mind.

196
00:12:11,900 --> 00:12:13,970
I came here to inquire not to confess.

197
00:12:15,190 --> 00:12:17,690
Is it known that Mr. Rochester is to be married?

198
00:12:18,510 --> 00:12:19,510
Yes.

199
00:12:20,069 --> 00:12:21,589
And to the beautiful Miss Ingram.

200
00:12:22,730 --> 00:12:23,730
Shortly?

201
00:12:24,930 --> 00:12:27,169
Appearances would warrant that conclusion.

202
00:12:28,169 --> 00:12:33,669
And, no doubt, though with an audacity that wants chastising out of you,

203
00:12:33,830 --> 00:12:34,949
you seem to question it.

204
00:12:35,610 --> 00:12:38,209
They will be a superlatively happy pair.

205
00:12:39,349 --> 00:12:43,889
He must love such a handsome, noble, witty, accomplished lady.

206
00:12:44,529 --> 00:12:46,230
And probably she loves him.

207
00:12:46,779 --> 00:12:50,050
Or, if not his person, at least his purse.

208
00:12:51,089 --> 00:12:55,669
I know she considers the Rochester estate eligible to the last degree.

209
00:12:56,639 --> 00:13:01,809
Though, God pardon me, I told her something on that point about an hour ago,

210
00:13:02,250 --> 00:13:04,250
which made her look wondrous grave.

211
00:13:05,559 --> 00:13:07,769
The corners of her mouth fell half an inch.

212
00:13:08,699 --> 00:13:11,470
I would advise her black-of-ice suit her to look out.

213
00:13:12,080 --> 00:13:16,970
If another comes, with a longer or clearer rent role, he's dished.

214
00:13:18,269 --> 00:13:22,290
But, mother, I did not come to hear Mr. Rochester's fortune.

215
00:13:23,444 --> 00:13:27,330
I came to hear my own, and you have told me nothing of it.

216
00:13:28,580 --> 00:13:30,250
Your fortune is yet doubtful.

217
00:13:31,209 --> 00:13:35,069
When I examined your face, one trait contradicted another.

218
00:13:36,209 --> 00:13:40,269
Chance has meted you a measure of happiness that I know.

219
00:13:41,769 --> 00:13:43,730
I knew it before I came here this evening.

220
00:13:44,580 --> 00:13:47,050
She has laid it carefully on one side for you.

221
00:13:47,959 --> 00:13:48,970
I saw her do it.

222
00:13:49,449 --> 00:13:52,790
It depends on yourself to stretch out your hand and take it up.

223
00:13:54,044 --> 00:13:57,050
But whether you will do so is the problem I study.

224
00:13:58,129 --> 00:13:59,129
Neil again on the rug.

225
00:14:00,269 --> 00:14:03,129
Don't keep me long, the fire scorches me.

226
00:14:04,430 --> 00:14:05,430
I knelt.

227
00:14:06,129 --> 00:14:10,230
She did not stoop towards me, but only gazed, leaning back in her chair.

228
00:14:11,190 --> 00:14:12,190
She began muttering.

229
00:14:13,029 --> 00:14:14,290
The flame flickers in the eye.

230
00:14:14,610 --> 00:14:15,989
The eye shines like dew.

231
00:14:16,589 --> 00:14:18,230
It looks soft and full of feeling.

232
00:14:19,110 --> 00:14:20,370
It smiles at my jargon.

233
00:14:21,010 --> 00:14:22,010
It is susceptible.

234
00:14:22,669 --> 00:14:25,669
Impression follows impression through its clear sphere.

235
00:14:26,349 --> 00:14:29,089
Where it ceases to smile, it is sad.

236
00:14:30,150 --> 00:14:33,538
An unconscious lassitude weighs on the lid that

237
00:14:33,538 --> 00:14:37,171
signifies melancholy resulting from loneliness.

238
00:14:37,690 --> 00:14:38,690
It turns from me.

239
00:14:39,610 --> 00:14:41,269
It will not suffer further scrutiny.

240
00:14:42,309 --> 00:14:47,709
It seems to deny, by a mocking glance, the truth of the discoveries I have

241
00:14:47,711 --> 00:14:53,010
already made, to disown the charge both of sensibility and chagrin.

242
00:14:54,135 --> 00:14:57,669
It's pride and reserve only confirm me in my opinion.

243
00:14:58,250 --> 00:14:59,790
The eye is favourable.

244
00:15:00,769 --> 00:15:04,050
As to the mouth, it delights at times in laughter.

245
00:15:04,889 --> 00:15:09,769
It is disposed to impart all that the brain conceives, though I dare say it

246
00:15:09,771 --> 00:15:12,290
would be silent on much the heart experiences.

247
00:15:14,330 --> 00:15:17,385
Mobile and flexible, it was never intended to be

248
00:15:17,387 --> 00:15:20,930
compressed in the eternal silence of solitude.

249
00:15:21,720 --> 00:15:24,879
It is a mouth which should speak much and smile

250
00:15:24,881 --> 00:15:28,330
often and have human affection for its interlocutor.

251
00:15:29,489 --> 00:15:30,910
That feature too is propitious.

252
00:15:32,220 --> 00:15:37,550
I see no enemy to a fortunate issue but in the brow, and that brow professes to say,

253
00:15:38,245 --> 00:15:43,629
I can live alone, if self-respect, and circumstances require me so to do,

254
00:15:44,629 --> 00:15:46,889
I need not sell my soul to buy bliss.

255
00:15:48,150 --> 00:15:53,669
I have an inward treasure born with me, which can keep me alive if all extraneous

256
00:15:53,671 --> 00:15:59,330
delights should be withheld, or offered only at a price I cannot afford to give.

257
00:16:00,819 --> 00:16:07,569
The forehead declares, reason sits firm and holds the reins, and she will not let

258
00:16:07,571 --> 00:16:11,010
the feelings burst away and hurry her to wild chasms.

259
00:16:11,910 --> 00:16:16,470
The passions may rage furiously, like true heathens as they are,

260
00:16:17,290 --> 00:16:20,370
and the desires may imagine all sorts of vain things.

261
00:16:21,290 --> 00:16:24,578
But judgment shall still have the last word in every

262
00:16:24,580 --> 00:16:28,069
argument, and the casting vote in every decision.

263
00:16:28,889 --> 00:16:34,410
Strong wind, earthquake shock, and fire may pass by, but I shall follow

264
00:16:34,411 --> 00:16:40,171
the guiding of that still small voice which interprets the dictates of conscience.

265
00:16:41,629 --> 00:16:45,370
Well said for it, your declaration shall be respected.

266
00:16:46,559 --> 00:16:52,349
I have formed my plans, right plans I deem them, and in them I have attended to the

267
00:16:52,351 --> 00:16:54,949
claims of conscience, the councils of reason.

268
00:16:56,330 --> 00:17:01,889
I know how soon youth would fade and bloom perish, if, in the cup of bliss offered,

269
00:17:02,569 --> 00:17:08,069
but one drag of shame, or one flavor of remorse were detected, and I do not want

270
00:17:08,071 --> 00:17:12,470
sacrifice, sorrow, disillusion, such is not my taste.

271
00:17:13,569 --> 00:17:17,370
I wish to foster not to blight, to earn gratitude,

272
00:17:17,370 --> 00:17:21,250
not to ring tears of blood, no nor of brine.

273
00:17:21,849 --> 00:17:26,750
My harvest must be in smiles, in endearments, in sweet, that will do.

274
00:17:28,180 --> 00:17:30,669
I think I rave in a kind of exquisite delirium.

275
00:17:31,790 --> 00:17:35,910
I should wish now to protract this moment at infinitum, but I dare not.

276
00:17:36,900 --> 00:17:39,410
So far I have governed myself thoroughly.

277
00:17:40,110 --> 00:17:43,368
I have acted as I inwardly swore I would act,

278
00:17:43,368 --> 00:17:47,031
but further might try me beyond my strength.

279
00:17:47,250 --> 00:17:48,949
Rise, miss air, leave me.

280
00:17:49,529 --> 00:17:50,949
The play is played out.

281
00:17:52,620 --> 00:17:53,620
Where was I?

282
00:17:54,360 --> 00:17:55,489
Did I wake or sleep?

283
00:17:56,569 --> 00:17:57,569
Had I been dreaming?

284
00:17:58,370 --> 00:17:59,370
Did I dream still?

285
00:18:00,389 --> 00:18:05,510
The old woman's voice had changed, her accent, her gesture, and all were

286
00:18:05,510 --> 00:18:09,910
familiar to me as my own face in a glass, as the speech of my own tongue.

287
00:18:10,879 --> 00:18:12,309
I got up, but did not go.

288
00:18:13,019 --> 00:18:18,089
I looked, I stirred the fire, and I looked again, but she drew her bonnet and her

289
00:18:18,091 --> 00:18:22,470
bandage closer about her face, and again beckoned me to depart.

290
00:18:24,275 --> 00:18:28,779
The flame illuminated her hand stretched out, roused now, and

291
00:18:28,781 --> 00:18:33,169
on the alert for discoveries, I at once noticed that hand.

292
00:18:34,059 --> 00:18:37,089
It was no more the withered limb of elde than my own.

293
00:18:38,040 --> 00:18:43,449
It was a rounded supple member, with smooth fingers symmetrically turned,

294
00:18:44,410 --> 00:18:50,410
a broad ring flashed on the little finger, and stooping forward, I looked at it,

295
00:18:50,709 --> 00:18:53,430
and saw a gem I had seen a hundred times before.

296
00:18:54,639 --> 00:18:58,129
Again, I looked at the face, which was no longer turned from me.

297
00:18:59,029 --> 00:19:04,889
On the contrary, the bonnet was doffed, the bandage displaced, the head advanced.

298
00:19:07,629 --> 00:19:09,489
Well, Jane, do you know me?

299
00:19:10,089 --> 00:19:12,839
Asked the familiar voice, only take off the red

300
00:19:12,841 --> 00:19:15,470
cloak, sir, and then, but the string is in a knot.

301
00:19:15,930 --> 00:19:16,930
Help me.

302
00:19:17,250 --> 00:19:18,250
Break it, sir.

303
00:19:18,650 --> 00:19:23,851
They're then off your landings, and Mr. Rochester stepped out of his disguise.

304
00:19:24,250 --> 00:19:26,589
Now, sir, what a strange idea.

305
00:19:28,040 --> 00:19:29,069
But well carried out, eh?

306
00:19:29,730 --> 00:19:30,730
Don't you think so?

307
00:19:31,569 --> 00:19:33,690
With the ladies, you must have managed well.

308
00:19:34,800 --> 00:19:35,800
But not with you.

309
00:19:36,230 --> 00:19:38,150
You did not act the character of a gypsy with me.

310
00:19:39,349 --> 00:19:41,589
What character did I act, my own?

311
00:19:42,870 --> 00:19:45,110
No, some unaccountable one.

312
00:19:45,970 --> 00:19:50,290
In short, I believe you have been trying to draw me out, or in.

313
00:19:51,120 --> 00:19:53,589
You have been talking nonsense to make me talk nonsense.

314
00:19:54,349 --> 00:19:55,690
It is scarcely fair, sir.

315
00:19:57,400 --> 00:19:58,400
Do you forgive me, Jane?

316
00:19:59,650 --> 00:20:01,430
I cannot tell till I've thought it all over.

317
00:20:02,089 --> 00:20:05,750
If on reflection, I find I have fallen into no great

318
00:20:05,752 --> 00:20:09,889
absurdity, I shall try to forgive you, but it was not right.

319
00:20:11,470 --> 00:20:15,089
Oh, you have been very correct, very careful, very sensible.

320
00:20:16,680 --> 00:20:19,830
I reflected and thought on the whole I had.

321
00:20:20,709 --> 00:20:21,709
It was a comfort.

322
00:20:22,529 --> 00:20:27,029
But indeed, I had been on my guard almost from the beginning of the interview,

323
00:20:27,730 --> 00:20:30,029
something of masquerade I suspected.

324
00:20:31,754 --> 00:20:34,269
I knew gypsies and fortune tellers did not express

325
00:20:34,271 --> 00:20:37,769
themselves as this seeming old woman had expressed herself.

326
00:20:38,745 --> 00:20:45,230
Besides, I had noted her famed voice, her anxiety to conceal her features.

327
00:20:46,495 --> 00:20:50,853
But my mind had been running on grace pool, that living

328
00:20:50,853 --> 00:20:54,510
enigma, that mystery of mysteries, as I considered her.

329
00:20:55,464 --> 00:20:57,309
I had never thought of Mr. Rochester.

330
00:20:59,139 --> 00:21:00,610
Well, said he.

331
00:21:01,389 --> 00:21:02,430
What are you musing about?

332
00:21:02,989 --> 00:21:04,849
What does that grave smile signify?

333
00:21:06,449 --> 00:21:08,330
Wonder and self-congratulation, sir.

334
00:21:09,300 --> 00:21:11,510
I have your permission to retire now, I suppose.

335
00:21:13,029 --> 00:21:14,190
No, stay a moment.

336
00:21:15,370 --> 00:21:18,529
And tell me what the people in the drawing room yonder are doing.

337
00:21:19,989 --> 00:21:21,830
Discussing the gypsy, I dare say.

338
00:21:23,150 --> 00:21:24,150
Sit down.

339
00:21:24,669 --> 00:21:26,190
Let me hear what they said about me.

340
00:21:27,400 --> 00:21:28,989
I had better not stay long, sir.

341
00:21:29,230 --> 00:21:30,569
It must be near 11 o'clock.

342
00:21:31,459 --> 00:21:34,783
Oh, are you aware, Mr. Rochester, that a stranger

343
00:21:34,785 --> 00:21:37,669
has arrived here since you left this morning?

344
00:21:39,110 --> 00:21:40,110
A stranger?

345
00:21:40,750 --> 00:21:40,930
No.

346
00:21:41,529 --> 00:21:42,529
Who can it be?

347
00:21:43,150 --> 00:21:44,230
I expected no one.

348
00:21:44,449 --> 00:21:45,449
Is he gone?

349
00:21:45,930 --> 00:21:46,930
No.

350
00:21:47,470 --> 00:21:50,328
He said he had known you long, and that he could take

351
00:21:50,330 --> 00:21:53,449
the liberty of installing himself here till you returned.

352
00:21:55,019 --> 00:21:57,430
The devil he did, did he give his name?

353
00:21:59,370 --> 00:22:00,849
His name is Mason, sir.

354
00:22:01,769 --> 00:22:07,050
And he comes from the West Indies, from Spanish town, in Jamaica, I think.

355
00:22:07,510 --> 00:22:09,550
Mr. Rochester was standing near me.

356
00:22:10,550 --> 00:22:13,330
He had taken my hand as if to lead me to a chair.

357
00:22:14,699 --> 00:22:20,290
As I spoke, he gave my wrist a convulsive grip, the smile on his lips froze,

358
00:22:21,309 --> 00:22:23,610
apparently a spasm caught his breath.

359
00:22:24,809 --> 00:22:27,370
Mason, the West Indies, he said.

360
00:22:28,239 --> 00:22:32,849
In the tone one might fancy a speaking automaton to announce its single words.

361
00:22:34,269 --> 00:22:40,930
Mason, the West Indies, he reiterated, and he went over the syllables three

362
00:22:40,930 --> 00:22:44,271
times, growing in the intervals of speaking whiter

363
00:22:44,273 --> 00:22:47,050
than ashes, he hardly seemed to know what he was doing.

364
00:22:48,750 --> 00:22:49,750
Do you feel ill, sir?

365
00:22:50,489 --> 00:22:51,489
I inquired.

366
00:22:52,010 --> 00:22:53,830
Jane, I've got a blow, I've got a blow, Jane.

367
00:22:54,330 --> 00:22:55,330
He's staggered.

368
00:22:55,449 --> 00:22:56,449
Oh, lean on me, sir.

369
00:22:57,449 --> 00:23:00,050
Jane, you offered me your shoulder once before.

370
00:23:00,830 --> 00:23:01,830
Let me have it now.

371
00:23:02,430 --> 00:23:02,870
Yes, sir.

372
00:23:03,190 --> 00:23:03,349
Yes.

373
00:23:04,035 --> 00:23:07,750
And my arm, he sat down and made me sit beside him.

374
00:23:08,610 --> 00:23:13,830
Holding my hand in both his own, he chafed it, gazing on me at the same

375
00:23:13,830 --> 00:23:16,910
time with the most troubled and dreary look.

376
00:23:18,239 --> 00:23:24,569
My little friend said he, I wish I were in a quiet island with only you, and trouble

377
00:23:24,571 --> 00:23:27,949
and danger and hideous recollections removed from me.

378
00:23:29,599 --> 00:23:30,599
Can I help you, sir?

379
00:23:31,500 --> 00:23:32,790
I'd give my life to serve you.

380
00:23:33,864 --> 00:23:38,250
Jane, if aid is wanted, I'll seek it at your hands.

381
00:23:38,769 --> 00:23:39,769
I promise you that.

382
00:23:40,779 --> 00:23:41,779
Thank you, sir.

383
00:23:41,949 --> 00:23:42,949
Tell me what to do.

384
00:23:43,050 --> 00:23:44,569
I'll try at least to do it.

385
00:23:45,910 --> 00:23:49,449
Fetch me now, Jane, a glass of wine from the dining room.

386
00:23:50,069 --> 00:23:56,290
They will be at supper there, and tell me if Mason is with them and what he is doing.

387
00:23:56,970 --> 00:23:57,970
I went.

388
00:23:59,809 --> 00:24:04,870
I found all the party in the dining room at supper, as Mr. Rochester had said.

389
00:24:05,910 --> 00:24:07,330
They were not seated at table.

390
00:24:08,169 --> 00:24:10,150
The supper was arranged on the sideboard.

391
00:24:11,169 --> 00:24:15,870
Each had taken what he chose, and they stood about here and there in groups,

392
00:24:16,699 --> 00:24:18,730
their plates and glasses in their hands.

393
00:24:19,629 --> 00:24:25,519
Everyone seemed in high glee, laughter and conversation were general and animated.

394
00:24:26,800 --> 00:24:30,514
Mr. Mason stood near the fire, talking to Colonel and Mrs.

395
00:24:31,383 --> 00:24:33,900
Dent, and appeared as Mary as any of them.

396
00:24:34,599 --> 00:24:35,739
I filled a wine glass.

397
00:24:36,639 --> 00:24:39,220
I saw Miss Ingram watch me frowningly as I did so.

398
00:24:39,760 --> 00:24:44,779
She thought I was taking a liberty, I dare say, and I returned to the library.

399
00:24:46,300 --> 00:24:50,006
Mr. Rochester's extreme pallor had disappeared,

400
00:24:50,008 --> 00:24:53,321
and he looked once more firm and stern.

401
00:24:54,300 --> 00:24:55,699
He took the glass from my hand.

402
00:24:56,800 --> 00:25:00,580
Here is to your health, minister and spirit, he said.

403
00:25:01,239 --> 00:25:03,180
He swallowed the contents and returned it to me.

404
00:25:05,044 --> 00:25:06,086
What are they doing, Jane?

405
00:25:07,400 --> 00:25:08,760
Laughing and talking, sir.

406
00:25:10,000 --> 00:25:14,019
They don't look grave and mysterious, as if they had heard something strange.

407
00:25:15,279 --> 00:25:16,279
Not at all.

408
00:25:16,650 --> 00:25:18,260
They are full of guests and gayity.

409
00:25:19,339 --> 00:25:20,339
And Mason?

410
00:25:21,110 --> 00:25:22,110
He was laughing too.

411
00:25:23,750 --> 00:25:28,680
If all these people came in a body and spat at me, what would you do, Jane?

412
00:25:29,629 --> 00:25:32,980
Turn them out of the room, sir, if I could, he half smiled.

413
00:25:34,720 --> 00:25:40,419
But if I were to go to them, and they only looked at me coldly and whispered

414
00:25:40,421 --> 00:25:42,832
sneeringly amongst each other, and then

415
00:25:42,832 --> 00:25:45,720
dropped off and left me one by one, what then?

416
00:25:46,540 --> 00:25:47,580
Would you go with them?

417
00:25:48,879 --> 00:25:50,139
I rather think not, sir.

418
00:25:50,879 --> 00:25:52,940
I should have more pleasure in staying with you.

419
00:25:54,260 --> 00:25:55,260
To comfort me?

420
00:25:56,160 --> 00:25:57,160
Yes, sir.

421
00:25:57,620 --> 00:25:59,400
To comfort you, as well as I could.

422
00:26:00,500 --> 00:26:05,680
And if they laid you under a ban for a daring to me, I probably should know

423
00:26:05,680 --> 00:26:10,019
nothing about their ban, and if I did, I should care nothing about it.

424
00:26:11,160 --> 00:26:14,139
Then you could dare censor for my sake.

425
00:26:15,489 --> 00:26:17,917
I could dare it for the sake of any friend who

426
00:26:17,919 --> 00:26:21,061
deserved my adherence, as you I am sure do.

427
00:26:22,459 --> 00:26:28,199
Go back now into the room, step quietly up to Mason, and whisper in his ear that Mr.

428
00:26:28,279 --> 00:26:30,160
Rochester has come and wishes to see him.

429
00:26:30,900 --> 00:26:32,779
Show him in here and then leave me.

430
00:26:33,940 --> 00:26:34,940
Yes, sir.

431
00:26:35,705 --> 00:26:36,720
I did his behest.

432
00:26:37,720 --> 00:26:41,220
The company all stared at me as I passed straight among them.

433
00:26:42,639 --> 00:26:47,480
I sought Mr. Mason, delivered the message and proceeded him from the room.

434
00:26:48,714 --> 00:26:52,139
I ushered him into the library, and then I went upstairs.

435
00:26:53,559 --> 00:26:57,112
At a late hour, after I had been in bed some time,

436
00:26:57,114 --> 00:27:00,220
I heard the visitors repair to their chambers.

437
00:27:00,739 --> 00:27:06,199
I distinguished Mr. Rochester's voice, and heard him say, this way, Mason,

438
00:27:06,800 --> 00:27:07,800
this is your room.

439
00:27:08,580 --> 00:27:09,580
He spoke cheerfully.

440
00:27:10,599 --> 00:27:12,699
The gay tones set my heart at ease.

441
00:27:13,980 --> 00:27:15,419
I was soon asleep.
